Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(about): show the build commit in Profile and the
 health route
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Profile's About row and /health both expose the running commit hash
and a build/boot timestamp, so a "did Telegram reload the new build?"
check is one curl or a glance at Profile instead of a guess.

vite.config defines __APP_COMMIT__ (RENDER_GIT_COMMIT or git rev-parse
--short HEAD, else "dev") and __APP_BUILT_AT__ (ISO build time). The
client reads them via src/lib/appInfo.ts; the server reads them via a
small server/appInfo.ts (the server is a separate tsc pipeline so the
client define does not reach it). /health adds commit + builtAt next
to the existing ok/uptime fields.

The Profile row keeps its single-line, dir=ltr form so the dot order
never scrambles in Persian.

