Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(team): news tab on the team page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ESPN's site API serves a per-league news feed (~6 articles, refreshed
throughout the day) at /{league}/news. Each article carries headline,
description, published, byline, images, a links.web.href URL, and a
categories[] array where the team entries use the SAME id this app
already uses for matches and rosters — so per-team news is a client-side
filter, no mapping.

New /api/leagues/:league/news route (in-memory 60s cache, one league
fetch shared across all teams in it). TeamPage gains a 5th tab "News"
(اخبار in FA) that calls the route with the team's id and renders a
vertical list of cards: thumbnail, headline, description, date+byline,
and a "Read on ESPN →" link that opens the article's web URL in a new
tab.

The team-specific ESPN path /teams/{id}/news returns 0 articles for
soccer (ESPN only populates it for US sports), so the league feed +
client filter is the only way.

